        <briefdescription>
<para>Initializes a new instance of the BoundedPriorityList&lt;TElement, TPriority&gt; class. Note: You should not have <emphasis>allocate</emphasis>  set to true, and the capacity set to a very large number. Especially if you will be creating and destroying many BoundedPriorityList&lt;TElement,TPriority&gt; very rapidly. If you ignore this advice you will create lots of memory pressure. If you don&apos;t understand why this is a problem you should understand the garbage collector. Please read: <ulink url="https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ee787088.aspx">https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ee787088.aspx</ulink>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>capacity</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The maximum capacity of the list.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>allocate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true, initializes the internal lists for the BoundedPriorityList&lt;TElement,TPriority&gt; with an initial capacity of <emphasis>capacity</emphasis> .</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
